#==============================================================================
# IWO (~2 at.% W:In2O3) FET, channel t = 6.3 nm  --  IWO_PHYSICS_CONSTRAINED_MODEL_V1  [IWO_material_model_v3]
# Generated by scripts/build_iwo_decks.py from config/iwo_material_model_v3.yaml (ONE material model for all
# thicknesses). Reduced electrical deck: ideal TiN gate / Pd S/D boundaries (equipotential metals, DC).
# MESH WIDTH = 1 um -> currents are A/um. Total 290-um device current = 290 x logged current. Never divide by 290.
# Cox = 8.9554e-07 F/cm^2 (HfO2 15 nm eps 19.57 + Al2O3 2 nm eps 9.0). Vd = 0.7 V, T = 300.0 K.
# Category labels: A intrinsic, B confinement, D bulk defects, E interface, F transport, G contacts, H numerical.
#==============================================================================
# [A] Eg_bulk = 3.05 eV | LITERATURE | Fan2021_Nanomaterials Sec.3 (different sputtered IWO device); dft_inputs.json bulk.TCAD_Eg_bulk_eV
# [B] dEg_QC(t) = 0.0724 eV | FITTED to COMPUTED DFT points (H-H 0.695/0.930/1.962 nm), no device data | a*t^-p, a=0.81431, p=1.31518 (dft_inputs.json laws.dEg_eV (dft_to_tcad_extract.py; relative residuals 0.003/-0.004/0.001); 6.3 and 13.2 nm are extrapolations)
# [A+B] EG300 = 3.1224 eV | CALCULATED | Eg_bulk + dEg_QC(t)
# [A] chi_bulk = 4.3 eV | LITERATURE | Fan2021_Nanomaterials Sec.3 (composition-mixing estimate); degenerate with the gate work function and Qf. DFT bulk-equivalent EA 4.776 eV (PBE, H-(001), dft_inputs.json bulk.EA_bulk_equivalent_eV) is termination-specific and NOT used
# [B] dEc(t) = 0.0622 eV | FITTED to COMPUTED DFT points (H-H 0.695/0.930/1.962 nm), no device data | a*t^-p, a=0.70147, p=1.31669 (dft_inputs.json laws.dEc_eV.fit3 (relative residuals 0.07/-0.09/0.027); 0.2816/0.0622/0.0235 eV at 2.0/6.3/13.2 nm; extrapolation spread 0.046-0.062 (6.3) and 0.013-0.024 eV (13.2) -> S6 low/high runs)
# [A+B] AFFINITY = 4.2378 eV | CALCULATED | chi_bulk - dEc(t)
# [A+B] m* = 0.2189 m0 | LITERATURE bulk 0.208 + increment law FITTED to COMPUTED DFT points (no device data) | dft_inputs.json laws.dm_m0 (PBE in-plane CB-mass increments film minus bulk 0.159 at H-H 0.695/0.930/1.962 nm = 0.1758/0.1221/0.0474 m0; residuals <= 0.2 %); m*(2.0/6.3/13.2 nm) = 0.2543/0.2189/0.2123 m0
# [A+B] NC300 = 2.5693e+18 cm^-3 | CALCULATED | 2(2 pi m* kT/h^2)^1.5; effective continuum DOS at 2 nm
# [A] NV300 = 1.000e+19 cm^-3 | ASSUMED | holes not solved
# [A] PERMITTIVITY = 9.3 - | MEASURED | Januar2026 SI Fig.S1 (C-V, IWO 9.30+/-0.04; the fab's measurement)
# [D] Nt(t) = 1.4059e+19 cm^-3 | FITTED shared (S4 launches); start Ns = 4e12 cm^-2 = V1 FITTED 2 nm anchor (Nt2 = Ns / 2 nm); surface/bulk placement is an S3 data-selected branch | Nt2*(2/t)^alpha, Nt2=4.4285e+19, alpha=1.0
# [D] NTA = Nt/WTA = 2.4578e+20 cm^-3/eV | CALCULATED | gTA(E)=NTA exp((E-Ec)/WTA); integral = NTA*WTA*(1-exp(-Eg/WTA))
# [D] WTA (kTt) = 0.0572 eV | FITTED shared (S4 launches); start = V1 FITTED 2 nm value | Tt = 664 K; shared across thickness
# [D] deep acceptor Gaussian = 5e+16 at Ec-0.6 eV, W=0.15 cm^-3/eV | ASSUMED (V2 continuity; Fan2021 range 2.5-3.7e16 for a different device); zero in S6 | 
# [D] Nd_eff(t) = 2.5000e+17 cm^-3 | FITTED V1 donor amplitude, kept fixed; constant thickness dependence ASSUMED (effective electrically active donor density, NOT the W concentration); x0.1 / x10 in S6 | Nd0*(1+(t/tc)^k), Nd0=2.5e+17, tc=1000000000.0 nm, k=4.0; NOT W concentration
# [E] interface acceptor sheet = 3e+11 at Ec-0.3 eV, W=0.12 eV cm^-2/eV | ASSUMED, shared across thickness; LITERATURE-scale Dit(HfO2/In2O3) ~6e11 cm^-2/eV (proxy; here IWO/Al2O3); zero in S6 | regularized 0.25 nm IWO layer at the Al2O3 interface: volume amplitude = sheet peak / 0.25 nm (numerically verified: layer /2 changes Id by 0.009 dec)
# [E] Qf = 1.6117e+12 cm^-2 | FITTED shared (one value for all films, carries the alignment offset dV0); S4 start = V2 FITTED value (least squares on the 2 and 13.2 nm anchors); profiled offline, range -1.4e12 .. 4.2e12 | dVfb = -q Qf/Cox = -0.2883 V
# [F] mu_band(t) = 26.4131 cm^2/Vs | FITTED shared law (mu_inf, ell profiled offline on the three thin films; start values pass through the V2 FITTED anchors); mass factor CALCULATED (LITERATURE 0.208 + DFT dm law) | shared law mu_inf*(0.208/m*(t))/(1+ell/t) at the S4 start values (listed films; the law below for any other thickness). MUN = 12.977 / 40.261 / 60.539 cm2/Vs
# [F] roughness factor = 0.9110 - | LITERATURE (Januar2026 Fig.5f, 2.87 A) | (1 - Dsr/t)^2, Dsr = 0.287 nm
# [F] MUN = mu_band*(1-Dsr/t)^2 = 24.0614 cm^2/Vs | CALCULATED | NOT inserted natively: ATLAS 5.28.1.R ignores MOBILITY updates between SOLVEs (EMPIRICAL, run_0008); the free/trapped partition is produced self-consistently by the DOS occupancy; IGZO.TOKYO (physics option) is the carrier-density branch
# [G] gate work function = 4.7 eV | ASSUMED (TiN 4.5-4.9 eV literature range); degenerate with Qf and chi -> held fixed | 
# [G] S/D = ideal Ohmic (no workfunction)  | ASSUMED; underconstrained (no TLM); Schottky branch = physics option schottky_sd | 
# [H] capture cross sections = 1e-15 cm^2 | ASSUMED | not identifiable from DC transfer curves
# [F] OPTION IGZO.TOKYO = GAMMA0 -0.31, TGAMMA 178.4 K, NCRIT 1e+20 cm^-3  | GAMMA0 FITTED if adopted (start LITERATURE default -0.31 / ASSUMED +0.30); TGAMMA LITERATURE default; NCRIT ASSUMED | PDF p.195-196; tft/tftex21
#==============================================================================
